    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the raw geometry, and so do I. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00304) runs 28.9 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a booked optimal of 24.0 km (EV-TRIP-00304) — an excess of 4.9 km, 20.4% of optimal — so both limbs of the POL-RD-01 test are passed (>0.8 km and >20%), and a deviation is established on this trip's own trace. The trace is sound for policy purposes: 247 fixes at a 10-second cadence, an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec 0, so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) are not engaged and the independent corroboration that clause demands of an impaired trace is not needed. The rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry TRP-00304 and the same pickup window.\n\nThe deviation is nevertheless exonerated under POL-RD-03. The bundle holds a full-weight LTA DataMall advisory (EV-ADVIS-00304-01) naming the very segment the optimal route traverses — 'Pan Island Expressway (PIE) towards Changi, Eunos Link to Bedok North Ave 4' — with a 17:40–21:00 window that brackets the whole trip, and its own text directs 'Divert via ECP'. That satisfies POL-RD-03(a) and (b). For limb (c), the actual route follows the diversion: the only ERP gantry charged is 'ECP (Fort Rd towards Changi)', flagged on_optimal_route false, and the nearest fix sits 0 m from it (fix 153), i.e. the vehicle left the PIE corridor for the ECP the advisory directed. The rider is right that the optimal route's own polyline is not in the record; limb (c) asks whether the actual route took the diversion, and the off-optimal ECP crossing shows that it did.\n\nExoneration is capped at min(measured 4.9 km, 1.30 × (shortest lawful alternative 27.5 − optimal 24.0) + 1.00 = 5.55 km) = 4.9 km, so the whole excess is justified and no residual distance excess survives. The closure-adjusted optimal is 24.0 + 4.9 = 28.9 km, and its duration is the booked 30.0 min scaled by 28.9/24.0 = 36.1 min. Recomputing the fare against that adjusted optimal: (3.80 + 0.75 × 28.9 + 0.28 × 36.1) × 1.0 (surge read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 on-optimal-route ERP = 36.38. Your charged total was 38.76, so the refund is 38.76 − 36.38 = 2.38, rounded up to SGD 2.40. The 1.00 off-route ERP line is already comprehended in that figure (POL-RD-09(1)) and is not added on top.\n\nThe rider's alternative figure of 7.80 (POL-RD-02 against the booked optimal) is rejected: it assumes the closure is not exonerated, and it is. Her POL-RD-11 point is accepted — the fare model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so no upfront-quote bar applies, and the ~$33 'quote' she recalls appears on no artifact and cannot be used. The driver's POL-RD-04 (rider-requested detour) argument is rejected as a source of exoneration: the only rider message is 'ok', which assents to a decision the driver had already announced and names nothing, and waypoint_hint is null, so that clause's corroboration test cannot run and it excludes no distance (POL-RD-14 does not apply either, since the route did follow the ECP). The driver's suggestion that the rider recovers nothing, or only the 1.00 ERP, is not accepted for the reason above. No POL-RD-06 uplift is available (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 260 completed trips — no pattern), so no conduct referral fires. There is no billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4): the ECP gantry was genuinely crossed, and the trip ends at Changi rather than originating there, so no airport surcharge is chargeable and none was charged. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires — trip ids match, timestamps neither disagree by 10 minutes nor run backwards, the trace is unimpaired, the advisory relied on is present and covers the window, and no charge line is orphaned — and confidence sits well above the 0.70 floor. The amount (2.40) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically.\n\nConfidence is capped under POL-GEN-02(2) at the minimum weight of the artifacts carrying the deciding facts — the GPS trace, trip record, fare breakdown and advisory all sit at weight 1.00 — so the cap is 1.00.",
